{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceLengthPinned","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceLengthPinned","imports":["lean:module:Init"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.interface_length_of_shift_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.interface_length_of_shift_eq","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceLengthPinned.lean#L90-L95","doc":"Contrapositive, in the form the `D(u)` check uses: if the compound shift\nmatches the recorded exponent for two interfaces, those interfaces have equal\nlength. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.shift_strict_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.shift_strict_mono","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceLengthPinned.lean#L83-L88","doc":"Substituting a longer interface strictly raises the normal-form shift,\nwhere `base` is the `Δ(β₁, β₂; A)` contribution of the two components.  This\nis what moves the `D(u)` exponent off its verified value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.colPole_not_faithful_of_zero_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.colPole_not_faithful_of_zero_step","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceLengthPinned.lean#L75-L81","doc":"The unit step is load-bearing.  If a generator contributed nothing to the\npole order, every word length would collapse to the same `α_shift` and the\ninterface would be entirely unconstrained. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.colPole_faithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.colPole_faithful","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceLengthPinned.lean#L68-L73","doc":"**The pinning.**  Pole order recovers word length exactly, so two\ninterface words of different lengths carry different `α_shift`.  The\ninterface slot in the shift decomposition is therefore not free: a substitute\nword is admissible only if it has the same length as the one it replaces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.colPole_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.colPole_one","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceLengthPinned.lean#L62-L66","doc":"On the all-column channel each generator has valuation `−1`, i.e.\ncontributes one to the pole order, so `α_shift` of a positive word IS its\nlength. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.colPole_eq_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.colPole_eq_mul","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceLengthPinned.lean#L53-L60","doc":"The pole order is linear in the word length. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.colPole","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.colPole","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceLengthPinned.lean#L46-L51","doc":"Pole order at `q = 0` of the all-column character of a positive braid\nword, accumulated one letter at a time.  `step` is the pole order contributed\nby a single generator; the column channel has `step = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}